  "id": "66837620-09c6-5aaf-9aac-5bebff84299a",
  "slug": "vermicelli-pudding",
  "name": "Vermicelli Pudding",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "A creamy, mild, and comforting pudding made of vermicelli (angel hair) pasta lightly spiced with cardamom and a few raisins is a beloved traditional food for Eid breakfast. It's good served warm or chilled.",
  "cuisine": "Middle Eastern Inspired",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Bring milk, sugar, and cardamom seeds to a boil in a saucepan; reduce heat to medium-low and simmer for 5 minutes. Stir broken vermicelli pasta and raisins into milk mixture and simmer until pasta is tender and the cream sauce has thickened, about 5 more minutes. Remove from heat and let stand until warm, about 15 minutes. If pudding is too thick, stir in a little milk."
    }
  ],
